<div class="sm-wizard__footer">
  <%# "More below" cue. Sits in the fade over this footer and scrolls the step on
      tap -- a visible control that did nothing when tapped would be worse than
      no control, especially on mobile where the fade alone is easy to miss.

      Hidden by CSS unless the wizard flags more content (wizard_scroll_controller),
      so it can never point at the end of the step.

      aria-hidden with tabindex="-1": it duplicates what scrolling already does,
      so it would be a redundant tab stop and redundant announcement. The
      negative tabindex keeps it unfocusable, which is what makes aria-hidden
      legitimate here rather than an ARIA violation. %>
  <button type="button"
          class="sm-wizard__scroll-cue"
          tabindex="-1"
          aria-hidden="true"
          data-action="click->wizard-scroll#scrollDown">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
      <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
    </svg>
  </button>

  <div class="flex items-center justify-between w-full px-4 sm:w-3/4 sm:mx-auto sm:px-0">
    <% if step > 1 %>
      <%# type="button" (not submit) so it can never become the form's
          implicit-submit default -- pressing Enter in a text field must
          advance (Next), never go back. Back navigation is driven by JS,
          which injects direction=back and submits; because the direction is
          not carried by this button's own name/value, the submit guard can
          safely disable it to prevent a Next-then-Back concurrent PUT. %>
      <button type="button"
              class="text-base font-semibold cursor-pointer text-blue-dark hover:underline disabled:opacity-60 disabled:cursor-not-allowed"
              data-action="click->smart-match-quiz#goBack"
              data-smart-match-quiz-target="backBtn">
        Go Back
      </button>
    <% else %>
      <div></div>
    <% end %>

    <button type="submit"
            form="quiz-form"
            class="px-10 py-3 text-sm font-bold tracking-wider text-white uppercase rounded-md cursor-pointer bg-blue-dark hover:bg-blue-medium disabled:bg-gray-5 disabled:opacity-60 disabled:cursor-not-allowed transition-colors"
            data-smart-match-quiz-target="submitBtn">
      <%= is_final_step ? "FIND MY MATCHES" : "NEXT" %>
    </button>
  </div>
</div>
